<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia govt study urges change to uranium levy.</title>
<headline>Australia govt study urges change to uranium levy.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Australian government report on Monday recommended reforms to the special safeguards levy paid by Australian uranium producers.</p>
<p>The report recommended the current fixed annual levy be ditched in favour of a per kilogram charge. The levy is aimed at covering the costs of safety measures and any future liabilities.</p>
<p>The government would decide on the report's recommendations within three months, the Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade, which participated in the study, said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
